.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt PKCS12_PARSE 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm PKCS12_parse
.Nd parse a PKCS#12 structure
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/pkcs12.h
.Ft int
.Fo PKCS12_parse
.Fa "PKCS12 *p12"
.Fa "const char *pass"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY **pkey"
.Fa "X509 **cert"
.Fa "STACK_OF(X509) **ca"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn PKCS12_parse
parses a PKCS12 structure.
.Pp
.Fa p12
is the
.Vt PKCS12
structure to parse.
.Fa pass
is the passphrase to use.
If successful the private key will be written to
.Sy *pkey ,
the corresponding certificate to
.Sy *cert
and any additional certificates to
.Sy *ca .
.Sh NOTES
Each of the parameters
.Fa pkey ,
.Fa cert ,
and
.Fa ca
can be NULL in which case the private key, the corresponding
certificate, or the additional certificates, respectively, will be
discarded.
If any of
.Fa pkey
and
.Fa cert
is non-NULL the variable it points to is initialized.
If
.Fa ca
is non-NULL and
.Sy *ca
is NULL a new STACK will be allocated.
If
.Fa ca
is non-NULL and
.Sy *ca
is a valid STACK then additional certificates are appended in the given
order to
.Sy *ca .
.Pp
The
.Sy friendlyName
and
.Sy localKeyID
attributes (if present) on each certificate will be stored in the
.Sy alias
and
.Sy keyid
attributes of the
.Vt X509
structure.
.Pp
The parameter
.Fa pass
is interpreted as a string in the UTF-8 encoding.
If it is not valid UTF-8, then it is assumed to be ISO8859-1 instead.
.Pp
In particular, this means that passwords in the locale character set (or
code page on Windows) must potentially be converted to UTF-8 before use.
This may include passwords from local text files, or input from the
terminal or command line.
Refer to the documentation of
.Xr UI_OpenSSL 3 ,
for example.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn PKCS12_parse
returns 1 for success and zero if an error occurred.
.Pp
The error can be obtained from
.Xr ERR_get_error 3
.Sh BUGS
Only a single private key and corresponding certificate is returned by
this function.
More complex PKCS#12 files with multiple private keys will only return
the first match.
.Pp
Only
.Sy friendlyName
and
.Sy localKeyID
attributes are currently stored in certificates.
Other attributes are discarded.
.Pp
Attributes currently cannot be stored in the private key
.Vt EVP_PKEY
structure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr d2i_PKCS12 3 ,
.Xr passphrase-encoding 7
